                <fr:addr>sss-000D</fr:addr>
                <fr:route>/sss-000D.xml</fr:route>
                <fr:title text="Semantic Category Examples">Semantic Category Examples</fr:title>
                <fr:taxon>Definition</fr:taxon>
                <fr:meta name="source">
                  <fr:link href="/dougherty-1993.xml" title="Closed Categories and Categorial Grammar" addr="dougherty-1993" type="local">[dougherty-1993]</fr:link>
                </fr:meta>
              </fr:frontmatter>
              <fr:mainmatter>
                <html:p>The only concrete example proposed by Dougherty give semantics in a presheaf category over a set of possible worlds. One of our insights is that by taking this to be presheaves over strings themselves, then we recover a universal semantics.</html:p>
              </fr:mainmatter>
